    {
      "id": 11005,
      "name": "Putts",
      "username": "Putts",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/c5a1d2/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-08-17T20:44:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The Prime Wardens version of Haka has a power which states: \"Play a card. &nbsp;If that card has \"Haka\" in the title, you may apply its effects to a target other than Haka.\"</p><p>What exactly does \"its effects\" refer to? &nbsp;Does it refer to the entire text of the card, or only the part of the card which happens after the drawing/discarding?</p><p>In other words, if Haka wanted to use his power to play Haka of Restoration to heal up Fanatic, does Haka draw 2 cards and then discard 1 or more cards so that Fanatic regains health, or does Fanatic draw 2 cards and discard 1 or more cards to regain health?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:12.862Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 11003,
      "topic_slug": "clarification-needed-on-prime-wardens-haka",
      "display_username": "Putts",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
